-- title:
--   Source Lévy stopped nonlinear negative-generator L1 energy vanishes under adaptive predictable marked cutoffs
-- statement:
--   For the actual original spectrally negative Lévy process, killed dividend-controlled reserve and true predictable clock μ, a decreasing jointly predictable family of marked time-state-source sets with empty intersection has vanishing absolute L1 energy for the ruin-stopped nonlinear C2 Taylor generator kernel under any bounded predictable discount. The source ν on negative marks and canonical -1<z<0 compensation are preserved; random time-and-state-dependent cutoffs are allowed, and no intrinsic jump-count compensator is assumed.
-- source:
--   W7-07 source-specific adaptive predictable L1 cutoff convergence based on Proved original source discounted energy 26fe1474, by antitone lintegral convergence; supplies signed generator drift cutoff approximations for W7-08.

